  "id": "mixed-model-analysis-of-variance",
  "term": "mixed-model analysis of variance",
  "definition": "Mixed-model analysis of variance is a statistical method used when a study includes both between-subjects factors, such as different groups, and within-subjects factors, such as repeated measurements over time. It tests effects across both kinds of comparisons in the same analysis.",
